        definition:
          'Inductor current and capacitor voltage cannot change instantaneously, because doing so would require infinite voltage or infinite current respectively and therefore infinite power. From this follow the equivalent models used at the two extremes: an initially relaxed inductor behaves as an open circuit at t = 0+ and as a short circuit at steady state, while an initially relaxed capacitor behaves as a short circuit at t = 0+ and as an open circuit at steady state. An element with a non-zero initial value is replaced by its ideal counterpart in series or parallel with a source carrying that value.',
