        definition:
          'Putting the module together: a circuit is analysed before switching to obtain the initial conditions, redrawn at t = 0+ to find any discontinuous quantities, analysed at steady state for the final conditions, and its time constant computed from the resistance seen by the storage element. The response follows from the three-quantity formula with no calculus. A complete solution also states which quantities jumped and why, and accounts for the stored energy, since those two checks catch most errors before they propagate.',
        takeaway: 'Four small analyses and one formula give the complete response — and the energy account is the check that it is right.',
