        code: { lang: 'math', src: 'f(t) periodic with period T\n\nF1(s) = transform of the FIRST PERIOD only\n\nF(s) = F1(s) / ( 1 - exp(-s*T) )\n\nDerivation: 1 + e^-sT + e^-2sT + ... = 1/(1 - e^-sT)\n            geometric, converges for Re(s) > 0\n\nThe exp(-sT) gives infinitely many poles: the harmonics.' },
