      'Built from TB1 Chapters 11 and 13, which the syllabus names. The two halves share a theme of encapsulation. Balanced three-phase analysis works because symmetry lets one phase stand for three, and the module begins by removing that symmetry to show what the shortcut was hiding — chiefly the neutral shift that appears the moment the return path is removed. The two-port half then builds encapsulation deliberately: a network of any complexity is replaced by four parameters that fully describe what it does at its terminals, which is the same abstraction Thevenin provided for one port extended to two.',
