        definition:
          'An unbalanced delta load is the easier of the two configurations because each branch sits directly across a line voltage, and the line voltages are fixed by the source regardless of the load. Each phase current is therefore its line voltage divided by its own branch impedance, computed independently with no coupling at all. The line currents follow from applying KCL at each corner of the delta, and because the branch currents are unequal the line currents are no longer root three times the branch currents nor 30 degrees displaced, as they are in the balanced case.',
