        code: { lang: 'math', src: 'V1 = A*V2 - B*I2\nI1 = C*V2 - D*I2          I2 defined as LEAVING the network\n\nA = V1/V2  with I2 = 0    B = -V1/I2 with V2 = 0\nC = I1/V2  with I2 = 0    D = -I1/I2 with V2 = 0\n\nCascade:  [T_total] = [T1][T2][T3]...   in signal-flow order\n\nReciprocal network:  AD - BC = 1' },
        mistake: 'Students multiply cascaded transmission matrices in the wrong order, or treat the product as commutative. Matrix multiplication is order-dependent, and reversing two blocks in a chain generally gives a different and wrong answer.',
