        code: { lang: 'math', src: 'dZ = Z11*Z22 - Z12*Z21\n\nY11 =  Z22/dZ     Y12 = -Z12/dZ\nY21 = -Z21/dZ     Y22 =  Z11/dZ\n\nZ to ABCD:\n  A = Z11/Z21,  B = dZ/Z21,  C = 1/Z21,  D = Z22/Z21\n\nReciprocity:  Z12 = Z21,  Y12 = Y21,  AD - BC = 1' },
        mistake: 'Students invert each element individually when converting Z to Y. The correct operation is a matrix inverse, which mixes all four elements through the determinant and swaps the diagonal entries.',
        book: { chapter: 13, pages: '315-321' },
