        terms: ['worked evaluation', 'series connection', 'parallel connection', 'cascade connection', 'parameter addition'],
        definition:
          'Parameters are evaluated by applying the defining conditions to the actual circuit: open or short the far port and compute the required ratio by ordinary circuit analysis. The parameter sets then earn their keep in interconnection, because each connection type corresponds to a simple matrix operation. Two-ports in series add their Z matrices, two-ports in parallel add their Y matrices, and two-ports in cascade multiply their ABCD matrices. Choosing the parameter set to match the connection turns a network analysis problem into two-by-two matrix arithmetic.',
